      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the midpoint of a segment with given endpoints \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\), we use the midpoint formula:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nGiven the endpoints \\((6, 12)\\) and \\((0, -6)\\), we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{6 + 0}{2}, \\frac{12 + (-6)}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expressions inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{6}{2}, \\frac{12 - 6}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{6}{2}, \\frac{6}{2} \\right) = (3, 3)\n\\]\n\nThe coordinates of the midpoint are \\((3, 3)\\). To find the sum of the coordinates, we add them together:\n\n\\[\n3 + 3 = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coordinates of the midpoint is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
